id: dark
name: Dark
kind: battlefield
lightLevel: -1
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Hard to see. Awareness and Defense Value down 2(bT), Perception Skill Bonus down 2.
text: >
  * Dark (-1). Reduce your Awareness and Defense Value by 2(bT) and reduce the Skill
  Bonus for your Perception Skill by 2.

---

# Two kinds of number, not one: the two Combat values are taken in (bT) and the Skill
# Bonus is taken flat. That is what the entry says, and it is the same split the Skill
# Check rules make everywhere - a Botch on a Skill Check is a flat 2 where every other roll
# loses 2(bT).
#
# (bT) rather than (T), so a Transformation does not make the dark easier to see in.

[passive]
awareness -= 2(bT);
defenseValue -= 2(bT);
skill.perception.bonus -= 2;
